  "label": "Dog's aggressive expression mapped to the speaker's hatred",
  "description": "The visual of the Shiba Inu dog snarling with its mouth open and teeth bared is mapped onto the textual statement 'i hate women so much'. The dog's aggressive expression serves as a visual metaphor for the speaker's supposed rage or hostility toward women, amplifying the hateful message through the common meme trope of using animal aggression to represent human emotion. This mapping relies on the audience's understanding that the dog's expression conveys anger, which is then analogically projected onto the speaker's stated emotion.",
